scsi: lpfc: Update correct ndlp refcnt when rejecting an unsolicited PLOGI

jira KERNEL-1940
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.187.1.el8_10
commit-author Nigel Kirkland <nkirkland2304@gmail.com>
commit 8dbdaf88f4b991cb5b0e178fa18deefcb1380207
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.187.1.el8_10/8dbdaf88.failed

The domain controller FC_ID can change whenever a fabric switch with an
ISL link is replaced or the admin reconfigures the fabric switch with
active links. In such situations, reference count updates should be
applied to the correct nodelist structure.

	Signed-off-by: Nigel Kirkland <nkirkland2304@gmail.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261013001648.62289-8-nkirkland2304@gmail.com
	Signed-off-by: Martin K. Petersen (Oracle) <mkp@kernel.org>
(cherry picked from commit 8dbdaf88f4b991cb5b0e178fa18deefcb1380207)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	drivers/scsi/lpfc/lpfc_els.c
